              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "39133002"
            }
          ],
          "value": "The mutation restricts the growth in the presence of alpha-methyl-glucoside (alpha-MG) and 2-deoxyglucose, which are non-metabolizable glucose analogs that can cause phosphosugar stress (PubMed:23582330). The mutant exhibits decreased PNP phosphatase activity, elevated intracellular PNP concentrations and increased PNP sensitivity (PubMed:39133002). The PLP phosphatase activity is significantly reduced in the yigL mutant and nearly abolished in the ybhA-yigL double mutant (PubMed:39133002)"
        }
      ],
